 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🌾 KrishiMitra — Crop Recommender Model Training\n",
    "This notebook contains the complete training pipeline for the **XGBoost Crop Recommender** model used in the KrishiMitra agricultural intelligence platform. \n",
    "\n",
    "### Pipeline Steps:\n",
    "1. Install and import required libraries.\n",
    "2. Download the standard 2,200-sample Kaggle Crop Recommendation dataset.\n",
    "3. Encode crop target labels.\n",
    "4. Train an XGBoost Classifier.\n",
    "5. Evaluate performance with precision/recall classification metrics.\n",
    "6. Save the trained model and label encoder as `.pkl` files and download them."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 1: Install Dependencies\n",
    "Run the following cell to install XGBoost and other machine learning libraries on the Google Colab instance."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install xgboost scikit-learn pandas numpy joblib"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2: Load the Dataset\n",
    "We pull the standard crop recommendation dataset directly from a public repository. It contains N (Nitrogen), P (Phosphorus), K (Potassium), temperature, humidity, pH, and rainfall metrics for various crops."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder\n",
    "import xgboost as xgb\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, classification_report, confusion_matrix\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "\n",
    "# Direct URL to the dataset\n",
    "dataset_url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Gladiator07/Harvestify/master/Data-science/Data/crop_recommendation.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load the dataset\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(dataset_url)\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Dataset loaded: {df.shape[0]} rows, {df.shape[1]} columns\")\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 3: Inspect unique classes & class balance"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Crops distribution:\")\n",
    "print(df['label'].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 4: Preprocessing & Label Encoding\n",
    "We separate the features from the target crop labels and encode the labels into integer values (0-21)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Separate features and target\n",
    "X = df.drop('label', axis=1)\n",
    "y = df['label']\n",
    "\n",
    "# Encode the target labels\n",
    "le = LabelEncoder()\n",
    "y_encoded = le.fit_transform(y)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display class mappings\n",
    "print(\"Label Encoding Class Mappings:\")\n",
    "for idx, crop in enumerate(le.classes_):\n",
    "    print(f\"  {idx:2d} -> {crop}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save the label encoder to disk\n",
    "joblib.dump(le, 'label_encoder.pkl')\n",
    "print(\"\\n💾 Saved 'label_encoder.pkl'\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 5: Split Train and Test Sets"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X, y_encoded, test_size=0.2, random_state=42, stratify=y_encoded\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(f\"Training set size: {X_train.shape[0]} samples\")\n",
    "print(f"Test set size: {X_test.shape[0]} samples\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 6: Train the XGBoost Classifier\n",
    "We initialize and fit the XGBoost classifier model on our training partition."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"🚀 Training XGBoost Classifier...\")\n",
    "model = xgb.XGBClassifier(\n",
    "    n_estimators=150,\n",
    "    max_depth=6,\n",
    "    learning_rate=0.1,\n",
    "    random_state=42,\n",
    "    eval_metric='mlogloss'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
    "print(\"✅ XGBoost Model training complete!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 7: Model Evaluation\n",
    "We evaluate the trained model on our held-out test split and print out metrics."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "y_pred = model.predict(X_test)\n",
    "accuracy = accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred)\n",
    "print(f\"📈 Test Set Accuracy: {accuracy:.4f}\\n\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred, target_names=le.classes_))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 8: Save and Download the Artifacts\n",
    "We dump the trained model model to a file and run Google Colab's download utility to download both `crop_recommender_model.pkl` and `label_encoder.pkl` to your local computer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Dump model checkpoint\n",
    "joblib.dump(model, 'crop_recommender_model.pkl')\n",
    "print(\"💾 Saved model to 'crop_recommender_model.pkl'\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Trigger browser download of the files\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from google.colab import files\n",
    "    files.download('crop_recommender_model.pkl')\n",
    "    files.download('label_encoder.pkl')\n",
    "    print(\"📥 Download triggered successfully!\")\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    print(\"⚠️ Colab downloader not available (not running inside Colab). Files are saved locally on disk.\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
